11:T61c,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can international students study in Italy with a scholarship?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Possible routes include MAECI, regional DSU benefits, university merit awards, fee waivers and research funding. Eligibility, coverage and application ownership differ."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I study in Italy without IELTS?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Possibly, when the exact programme accepts another certificate or documented prior education in English. There is no country-wide IELTS waiver, so verify the programme's accepted evidence."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are Italian public universities free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not automatically. Fees can be reduced according to income, status or a waiver, but each university publishes its own calculation, deadlines and mandatory charges."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Universitaly the university application portal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually it is a later pre-enrolment step for eligible international applicants. You first follow the university's own admission instructions unless that institution explicitly states another route."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a scholarship guarantee an Italian student visa?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Admission, funding and the visa are separate decisions. The competent Italian diplomatic mission makes the visa decision using its current requirements."}}]}1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://aspirecompass.org/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Explore opportunities by country and region\",\"item\":